⚠ MODULE NOT FULLY CONNECTED — SUGGESTIONS
======================================================================
• Your seeds split into 137 components even on the full reference graph. This suggests biologically distinct seed subgroups. Consider: (a) reviewing whether all seeds belong to the same disease module, (b) running RWR separately per seed subgroup, or (c) increasing --k to give the walker more room to bridge them.
• 128 seeds have no edges to other seeds in the reference graph. These are likely poorly connected genes — check whether they should remain as seeds or be moved to a validation set.
• Bridging hit the cap (--max-bridge=1000). Try increasing it (e.g., --max-bridge 2000).
• LCC fallback was used — non-LCC components were discarded. If you want to preserve all genes, set --no-lcc-fallback and report the module as multi-component.
• Consider lowering MultiXrank's restart probability `r` (more diffusion) or tuning `delta` (more inter-layer jumping) in script 1, then re-running.
• Check that pathway and LR layers are well-populated: sparse inter-layer edges limit the walker's ability to bridge disconnected seed clusters.

